WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:06.149
Writer-director Richard Linklater's 1993 film
Dazed and Confused is considered to be a cult

00:00:06.149 --> 00:00:06.740
classic.

00:00:07.189 --> 00:00:12.520
The ultimate ensemble film, this high school
comedy featured a host of up-and-coming actors,

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:16.760
and in the twenty-something years since it
arrived in theaters, some of those kids have

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.820
grown up to become A-list celebrities... while
others have faded into obscurity.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.820
Here's what the cast of Dazed and Confused
looks like today.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.100
Nicky Katt

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:32.280
In a movie filled with cool and lovable characters,
Nicky Katt's Clint Bruno stands apart as one

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:37.970
who's downright scary, and thanks to his intimidating
turn as the angry alpha male, actor Nicky

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.430
Katt has faced some typecasting over the years.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:41.430
He told IGN,

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:46.070
"I mean, everyone…says that the bad guys
are the most fun, but I've definitely gone

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:50.610
through streaks where that's all people wanted
me to play, the bad guy, especially after

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:51.720
Dazed and Confused."

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.940
Nevertheless, Katt has managed to carve out
a pretty impressive career, and has kept in

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.870
touch with some of his Dazed and Confused
comrades.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:03.850
Among countless other roles, he's played a
pretty awful guy in the Matthew McConaughey

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:09.270
movie A Time to Kill, joined up with Richard
Linklater for SubUrbia, and even starred in

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:13.020
Adam Goldberg's 1998 indie film Scotch and
Milk.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.920
Apparently, he's forgiven the guy for slugging
him in the nose.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.400
Jason London

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:22.590
If you had to pick a main character in Dazed
and Confused, it'd be football star Randall

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.500
"Pink" Floyd, played by Jason London.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:29.150
At first, it seemed like London was poised
for stardom, but the A-list life has eluded

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:30.880
the actor so far.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:35.579
After Dazed and Confused, London showed up
in a series of little-seen features, made-for-TV

00:01:35.579 --> 00:01:38.729
movies, and TV shows like Tales from the Crypt.

00:01:38.729 --> 00:01:43.829
As far as big roles go, he was the leading
man in The Rage: Carrie 2, the critically

00:01:43.829 --> 00:01:47.400
derided, unnecessary sequel to Brian De Palma's
horror classic.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:48.660
Anthony Rapp

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:54.040
One of the smartest guys in school, Tony Olson
is the poker-playing intellectual with really

00:01:54.049 --> 00:01:56.579
weird dreams about Abraham Lincoln.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:01.320
Actor Anthony Rapp got his start in the Elisabeth
Shue comedy Adventures in Babysitting.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:08.259
Later on, he'd play in Six Degrees of Separation,
appear in TV shows like The X-Files, and reunite

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:13.120
with Dazed and Confused co-star Adam Goldberg
as one of Russell Crowe's buddies in A Beautiful

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:13.620
Mind.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.860
However, Rapp is best known for his work on
Broadway.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:22.030
The Illinois-born actor starred with Idina
Menzel in the 2014 show If/Then and toured

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:24.060
the country in Little Shop of Horrors.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:28.940
And of course, Rapp was one of the original
actors in the Tony-award winning musical Rent,

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.190
even appearing in the 2005 movie adaptation.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:37.230
The actor also made headlines in late 2016
when it was announced he'd be playing Lt.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:42.310
Stamets in Star Trek: Discovery, the first
character in the long-running franchise originally

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:43.640
created to be gay.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.360
Rory Cochrane

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:50.840
Everybody's favorite stoner, Ron Slater is
one of the most iconic characters in Richard

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.520
Linklater's entire filmography.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:57.620
This long-haired pothead stole the show, and
that's 100 percent thanks to Rory Cochrane,

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:01.680
the only guy who could ever convince you that
George Washington was involved in an alien

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:02.180
cult.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:06.500
This wasn't the last time Cochrane would play
a spaced-out hippie for Linklater.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:10.410
In 2006, the actor showed up as a junkie in
A Scanner Darkly.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:16.040
He also played a Doors-quoting biker alongside
his future wife Renee Zellweger in Empire

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:21.190
Records, and he later joined up with CSI:
Miami, playing the part of Tim Speedle, a

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:25.480
trace evidence and impressions expert who
wasn't too big on proper gun maintenance.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:30.860
More recently, he's popped up in a smattering
of high-profile movies like Public Enemies,

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:32.540
Argo, and Black Mass.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:34.620
Marissa Ribisi

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:40.040
The brains behind the "every other decade"
theory, Cynthia Dunn spends most of her time

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:42.890
hanging out with fellow nerds Mike and Tony.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:47.031
She's a lot more laid back than the rest of
her trio, and by the end of the film, she's

00:03:47.031 --> 00:03:49.830
got plans to check out an Aerosmith concert.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:55.040
The twin sister of actor Giovanni Ribisi,
Marissa has continued to pop up in TV shows

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.400
like Friends and Grace Under Fire.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:03.530
She hasn't done a lot of acting since 2003,
but in 2008, Ribisi teamed up with Sophia

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:09.000
Banks to form Whitley Kros, a fashion line
that showed up in the likes of Vogue and ELLE.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.080
Ribisi is also a busy mom, having two kids
with the musician Beck.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:14.900
Adam Goldberg

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:20.170
The snarkiest character in Dazed and Confused,
Mike Newhouse, played by Adam Goldberg, is

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:23.260
the wisecracking senior who punches a bully
in the face.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:28.460
Goldberg went on to have one of the most successful
careers of anyone involved with Dazed and

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:28.960
Confused.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:31.600
Consider his filmography: A Beautiful Mind.

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:32.970
Saving Private Ryan.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:33.680
Waking Life.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:38.879
These are just a few of the films rounding
out his resume, but Goldberg is also equally

00:04:38.879 --> 00:04:44.360
comfortable appearing on TV in shows like
Entourage, ABC's short-lived cop comedy The

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:47.889
Unusuals, and even as a nutty roommate in
Friends.

00:04:47.889 --> 00:04:52.580
In addition to acting, Goldberg has directed
four of his own movies, and he's released

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:53.460
three albums.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:58.860
Oddly enough, Goldberg isn't all that enamored
with the role of Mike Newhouse, he told Uproxx

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:02.449
that he considers his performance to be "some
of [his] worst acting ever."

00:05:02.449 --> 00:05:06.920
Considering it was only his third feature
film, he's probably being a bit hard on himself.

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:08.520
Wiley Wiggins

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:13.330
Whether he's trying to escape from a gang
of paddle-wielding seniors or get it on with

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:16.849
an older girl, Mitch Kramer is the kid we're
all cheering on.

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:20.949
And in that role is Austin resident Wiley
Wiggins, who's made an interesting life for

00:05:20.949 --> 00:05:23.680
himself in the years since Dazed and Confused.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:27.680
He's shown up in a couple of small films,
but his next biggest role when he signed up

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.360
for another Richard Linklater flick, Waking
Life.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:34.420
Wiggins hasn't done any professional acting
since 2013.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:37.279
Instead, he makes his living in the tech world.

00:05:37.279 --> 00:05:42.400
He's also big into the indie gaming scene,
helping to found a video game collective known

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:44.120
as Juegos Rancheros.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:50.320
Created in 2011, the group hosts an annual
Austin festival called Fantastic Arcade and

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:54.600
operates an arcade and art space known as
the Museum of Human Amusement.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:56.160
Parker Posey

00:05:56.680 --> 00:06:01.080
Time Magazine named her the "Queen of the
Indies," but before Parker Posey became a

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:06.150
darling of the indie scene, she terrified
freshmen students as Darla Marks, the meanest

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:07.100
girl in school.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:12.500
Of course, prior to landing the role of Darla,
Posey was a regular on the soap opera As the

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:13.320
World Turns.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:18.580
Later on, she appeared in the cult classic
Party Girl, and Richard Linklater's SubUrbia.

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:22.879
But while she's had a few mainstream roles
here and there—like Lex Luthor's moll in

00:06:22.879 --> 00:06:27.900
Superman Returns—she's probably best known
for her collaborations with improv extraordinaire,

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:30.650
Christopher Guest, starring in four of his
films.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:35.150
Posey fans should keep an eye out for Netflix's
upcoming Lost in Space series, in which the

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:39.380
actress will play Dr. Smith, a gender-bending
take on the classic character.

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:41.120
Christin Hinojosa

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:46.560
After being publicly humiliated and slathered
with condiments, Sabrina Davis spends the

00:06:46.569 --> 00:06:51.349
rest of her evening proving she's more mature
than her 14 years might otherwise indicate.

00:06:51.349 --> 00:06:56.699
Her real-life counterpart, Christin Hinojosa,
has a similarly impressive attitude, only

00:06:56.699 --> 00:07:00.419
instead of hanging out with the cool kids,
she spends her time helping those who are

00:07:00.419 --> 00:07:01.909
far less fortunate.

00:07:01.909 --> 00:07:06.949
Hinojosa appeared in a few more projects after
Dazed and Confused, like the TV show Clueless

00:07:06.949 --> 00:07:10.229
and the made-for-TV movie The Computer Wore
Tennis Shoes.

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:13.200
However, Hinojosa quickly grew "bored" with
acting.

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:16.479
As she explained to the Third Coast Press
in 2005,

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:22.360
"I was doing silly TV movies and sitcom work….With
the type of work I was doing, I knew I wasn't

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:25.760
that great at it, and I wasn't being of any
use to this planet I love."

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:30.760
Inspired to do something more, she became
involved with the anti-war group called the

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:36.430
American Friends Service Committee, coordinating
a multimedia exhibit called Eyes Wide Open:

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:41.270
Beyond Fear, which displayed a pair of boots
for every American soldier killed in Iraq.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:47.460
As recently as 2013, Hinojosa worked as a
director of philanthropy for Solidarity Bridge,

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:51.560
a group that provides medical equipment for
people in Bolivia and Paraguay.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:53.640
Milla Jovovich

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:58.360
One of the biggest stars to come out of Dazed
and Confused, Milla Jovovich left a lasting

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:01.550
impression as Michelle, the guitar-strumming
stoner.

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:07.360
Perhaps more than anyone else, Dazed and Confused
had a direct impact on Jovovich's life: the

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:12.460
16-year-old married her 20-year-old costar,
Shawn Andrews, and the couple remained hitched

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:14.840
for a grand total of two months.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:19.490
Before Dazed and Confused, she scandalized
audiences in Return to the Blue Lagoon, and

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:22.400
she stole the spotlight as Leeloo in The Fifth
Element.

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:26.680
But if you're at all familiar with zombie
flicks, then you're well aware that Jovovich

00:08:26.689 --> 00:08:32.110
is best known for her role as the tough-as-nails
Alice from the Resident Evil franchise.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:37.469
Jovovich has also worked as an official spokesmodel
for L'Oréal, started her own fashion line,

00:08:37.469 --> 00:08:40.329
and even made a name for herself in the music
industry.

00:08:40.329 --> 00:08:42.780
As for her acting career goes, she's far from
done.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:44.540
Ben Affleck

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:49.260
Maybe he's a good guy to have blocking for
you, but Fred O'Bannion is the kind of person

00:08:49.269 --> 00:08:53.300
you love to hate, and that's all thanks to
Batman himself, Ben Affleck.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.500
It's no secret what he's up to today.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:59.850
He may have had his show business start appearing
in Burger King commercials, but after beating

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:04.779
up on Wiley Wiggins, Affleck continued struggling
in the film industry until finally winning

00:09:04.779 --> 00:09:07.430
an Oscar for co-writing Good Will Hunting.

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:12.070
With that statuette in hand, the actor went
on to star in blockbusters like Armageddon

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.200
and Pearl Harbor.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:18.680
Affleck turned his career around after starring
in bombs like Daredevil and Gigli by stepping

00:09:18.699 --> 00:09:24.209
behind the camera, directing movies such as
Gone Baby Gone, and the Oscar-winning Argo.

00:09:24.209 --> 00:09:28.580
And of course, he's also been donning Bruce
Wayne's cape and cowl and mercilessly beating

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.440
anyone unlucky enough to get in his way.

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:32.680
Hey, that sounds kind of like Fred O'Bannion.

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:34.780
Matthew McConaughey

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:39.980
A-list actor Matthew McConaughey keeps getting
older, but David Wooderson stays the same

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:40.480
age.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:45.220
Really, McConaughey doesn't need an introduction,
but even though he's been in tons of films,

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:47.400
Wooderson is still his most memorable character.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:52.060
Since then, McConaughey has become a major
Hollywood player, starting off in films like

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:56.950
Contact and A Time to Kill before charming
it up in a series of rom-coms like The Wedding

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:59.120
Planner and Failure to Launch.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:04.389
More recently, the actor has been wowing critics
and audiences alike in roles in True Detective

00:10:04.389 --> 00:10:06.100
and Dallas Buyers Club.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:08.980
In other words, it seems the man is doing
pretty okay.

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:10.360
Or, as he'd say it…

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:13.140
"alright alright alright"

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:14.750
Thanks for watching!

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:17.700
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:20.259
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

